<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Armenia (Orontid)</h1><p class="st-meta">570 BCE – 200 BCE (approx.) · capital Armavir</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first Armenian dynasty, the Orontids or Yervandunis, ruled Armenia as Persian satraps and then as kings for over three centuries before the Seleucids took over.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-urartu">Kingdom of Urartu</a>, Armenian-speaking groups dominated the highlands. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orontid-dynasty">Orontid</a> family appears as governors of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrapy</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/armenia">Armenia</a> under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/behistun-inscription">Behistun inscription</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-i">Darius I</a> records fighting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> in 521 BCE. The traditional start of the dynasty in the 6th century BCE is uncertain.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orontid-dynasty">Orontids</a> ruled as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satraps</a> closely tied to the Persian court, sending horses as tribute, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xenophon">Xenophon</a> described the villages and wheat beer of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/armenia">Armenia</a> in 401 BCE. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a>, they ruled as effectively independent kings from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armavir-ancient-city">Armavir</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yervandashat">Yervandashat</a>. Their culture blended Iranian religion and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aramaic">Aramaic</a> administration with local traditions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 200 BCE the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orontes-iv">Orontes IV</a> and divided the land between his generals <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxias-i">Artaxias</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zariadres">Zariadres</a>. After the Seleucid defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-magnesia">Magnesia</a> in 190 BCE, Artaxias founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-armenia-artaxiad">Kingdom of Armenia (Artaxiad)</a>, which kept many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orontid-dynasty">Orontid</a> traditions.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-armenia-orontid.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Armenia (Orontid)" width="320" height="208"><figcaption>Image: Armenica.org · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yervanduni_Armenia,_IV-II_BC.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>570 BCE – 200 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Armavir</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Orontes I, Orontes III, Orontes IV</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Iranian-influenced Armenian paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Armenian; Aramaic in administration</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/armenia">Armenia</a>, <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Orontid Armenia, Satrapy of Armenia, Yervanduni Armenia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-385&amp;focus=kingdom-of-armenia-orontid" aria-label="Kingdom of Armenia (Orontid) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5763 742 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Armenia (Orontid) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6083 998L6077 1051M6083 998L6231 1174M6083 998L6140 1251M6083 998